    ["cad_files",
    ".ICS",
    "IronCAD 3D Scene",
    "3.6",
    "An ICS file is a calendar file saved in a universal calendar format used by several email and calendar programs, including Microsoft Outlook, Google Calendar, and Apple Calendar. It allows users to share calendar information on the web and over email. For example, when users send a meeting request to others, they can share ICS files with them, who can import the meetings details into their calendars. ICS file open in Apple Calendar In 1998, the Internet Engineering Task Force created the iCalendar, or ICS, file format. ICS files are plain text files that contain information about a calendar event, including the events: Title Summary and description Start and end times Location Alert trigger The ICS format is a universal calendar file format that all popular calendar applications, including Microsoft Outlook, Apple Calendar, Google Calendar, and Mozilla Thunderbird Lightning Calendar, create and recognize. Because all popular calendar applications can use ICS files to add event details to a calendar, ICS files are the most common type of files used to exchange calendar information. Most commonly, office workers and other professionals use ICS files to send each other meeting requests. You may also receive ICS reminders for an upcoming birthday, holiday, trip, party, or other events. You can open an ICS file with various applications. For example, if you have a calendar application, such as Microsoft Outlook, Google Calendar, or Apple Calendar, installed on your device, you can double-click an ICS file to import the event details the file contains into your calendar. If necessary, you can also manually import an ICS file into your calendar app. For example, to import an event into the web version of Google Calendar: Click the Gear icon that appears in the programs upper right-hand side. Select Settings → Import & export. Select Import and import your ICS file. The event(s) it contains will be added to your calendar. If you are having trouble importing your ICS file into a calendar application, you can open the file in any text editor, such as Microsoft Notepad (Windows) or Apple TextEdit (Mac), to view the event information it contains. For example, you can see the events start and end times (including time zone) listed in the files DTSTART and DTEND lines. While opening an ICS file with a text editor is not the best way to view an events details, it does allow you to view the information without a calendar application. You can convert an ICS file to a CSV file with a free online ICS to CSV converter, such as Indigoblue. ICS to CSV Converter or ProjectWizards ICS to CSV Converter. By converting an ICS file to a CSV file, you can import a calendar event into Microsoft Excel or another spreadsheet program. Android Google Calendar. Windows Microsoft Outlook 365. Mozilla Thunderbird Lightning Calendar. Any text editor Mac Apple Calendar Included with OS. Mozilla Thunderbird Lightning Calendar. Flexibits Fantastical. Any text editor Linux Mozilla Thunderbird Lightning Calendar. Horde Kronolith. Claws Mail with vCalendar plugin. Any text editor Web Google Calendar. Indigoblue. ICS to CSV Converter. ProjectWizards ICS to CSV Converter. iOS Apple Calendar Included with OS. Google Calendar. Chrome OS Google Calendar. Google Chrome Text Included with OS. An ICS file is a 3D scene created by IronCAD, a 3D and 2D CAD application. It contains one or more parts or assemblies that include colors, textures, lighting effects, and other properties. IronCAD users primarily save 3D scenes as ICS files and 2D drawings as.ICD files. ICS file open in IronCAD 2022 IronCAD is a Windows CAD application that can create 2D and 3D models of real-life objects. Engineers primarily use IronCAD to design various objects for production, such as mechanical parts and furniture. When you save a 3D scene with IronCAD, the software creates an ICS file to store its contents. To create an ICS file, select Menu → File → New Scene. After modifying the scene, select Menu → File → Save or Save As.. NOTE: IronCAD saves ICS files to the following directory by default: Documents/​IRONCAD [version]. You can open ICS files with IronCAD in Windows by: Selecting Menu → File → Open.. Clicking the Open folder icon in the top toolbar Home tab. Windows IronCAD. An ICS file is an audio file created by the Sony ICD-R100 voice recorder. It contains recorded audio, usually a personal memo or a conversation between two or more people. For example, an ICS file might contain an interview conducted by a reporter. The Sony IC-R100 is a voice recorder that Sony released in 1999. It allowed users to record and play back voice recordings saved as messages. Each message was saved as an ICS file. Users could transfer messages from their IC-R100 to a Windows PC using ICD-PCLINK software. This allowed users to store and play ICS files on their PC. You can open an ICS file in Sony Digital Voice Player, a free ICS audio player for Windows. You can also open an ICS file in Windows Media Player with the Sony Player plug-in installed. Windows Sony Digital Voice Player. Microsoft Windows Media Player with Sony Player Plug-in Included with OS.",
    "Android Google Calendar. Windows Microsoft Outlook 365. Mozilla Thunderbird Lightning Calendar. Any text editor. Mac Apple Calendar Included with OS. Mozilla Thunderbird Lightning Calendar. Flexibits Fantastical. Any text editor. Linux Mozilla Thunderbird Lightning Calendar. Horde Kronolith. Claws Mail with vCalendar plugin. Any text editor. Web Google Calendar. Indigoblue. ICS to CSV Converter. ProjectWizards ICS to CSV Converter. iOS Apple Calendar Included with OS. Google Calendar. Chrome OS Google Calendar. Google Chrome Text Included with OS. Windows IronCAD. Windows Sony Digital Voice Player. Microsoft Windows Media Player with Sony Player Plug-in Included with OS.",
    "IronCAD can convert ICS files to many file types, including the following formats:.SAT - ACIS SAT 3D Model.X_T - Parasolid Model Part File.MODEL - CATIA 3D Model.CATPART - CATIA V5 Part.CATPRODUCT - CATIA V5 Assembly.IGS - IGES Drawing.STP - STEP 3D Model.STL - Stereolithography File.JPG - JPEG Image.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.TIF - Tagged Image To export an ICS file with IronCAD, select Menu → File → Export."],
    ["cad_files",
    ".RSM",
    "RouterSim Network Visualizer File",
    "3.6",
    "Script used by ARIS business reporting software; generates a report when run in the software and includes information about the database at the Model level, which is a logical division of the business database (other levels are Database, Group, and Object); used for generating business intelligence reports. Windows Software AG ARIS. Resume file created by Resume Deluxe, a program used for creating and auditing resumes; contains text, styles, images, formatting, and page layout data; used for creating resumes during the job application process. RSM files may be exported into.PDF,.RTF, ASCII text, and.HTML files using Resume Deluxe. Windows WinWay Resume Deluxe. Computer network layout created by Network Visualizer, a program used for computer network design and simulation; supports routers, switches, hosts, and other devices; often used in IT training environments for learning about different network configurations. Network Visualizer is available in several different versions, including CCNA, CCNP, CCENT, SWITCH, and ROUTE editions. The software is used to train for Cisco network professional certifications. Windows RouterSim CCNA Network Visualizer.",
    "Windows Software AG ARIS. Windows WinWay Resume Deluxe. Windows RouterSim CCNA Network Visualizer.",
    "?"],
    ["cad_files",
    ".BDL",
    "CoCreate Bundle File",
    "3.6",
    "A BDL file is a data file created by CoCreate CAD software programs such as CoCreate Modeling, SolidDesigner, and OneSpace Designer. It stores a bundle of all data for a 2D or 3D design and is used to save and load model data. CoCreate programs were superseded by PTC Creo in June 2011 when PTC Creo was released. PTC Creo still supports the BDL format. Windows PTC Creo.",
    "Windows PTC Creo.",
    "?"],
    ["cad_files",
    ".SCH",
    "gEDA Schematic File",
    "3.6",
    "An SCH file contains a schematic, or visual diagram, of a PCB (printed circuit board) created with EAGLE PCB design software. It stores symbols (for logic gates) connected by lines, which represent buses. EAGLE users often create actual circuit board (.BRD) files from SCH files. SCH file open in Autodesk EAGLE 9 Autodesk EAGLE (formerly CadSoft EAGLE) is a CAD application that professional electronics designers use to create PCB schematics and designs. EAGLE includes a schematic editor designers use to create electronic circuit schematics and save them as SCH files. After a designer creates a schematic, they can use EAGLE to place their schematic within a physical circuit board design. Those designs are saved as BRD files. NOTE: EAGLE stands for Easily Applicable Graphical Layout Editor.. You can open an SCH file in a variety of PCB design applications, including: Autodesk EAGLE (cross-platform) Altium Designer (Windows) If you do not have access to any of the above applications, the easiest way to view the circuit board schematic contained within an SCH file is to upload it to Altium 365 Viewer, a free, online CAD file viewer (web). Windows Autodesk EAGLE. Altium Designer. Mac Autodesk EAGLE. Linux Autodesk EAGLE. Web Altium 365 ViewerFree. Project file created by SuperCard, a visual authoring tool for Mac OS X; stores data for a help project, which contains indexable help content; used for extending the SuperCard Help System. Mac Solutions Etcetera SuperCard. Solutions Etcetera SuperCard Help. Schematic file created and used by gEDA, a collection of tools used to design PCB layouts and electronic schematics; contains data that makes up the schematic; includes the gEDA/gaf format version, pictures, and XY coordinates for nets, buses, and components. Electronic schematics consist of a collection of symbols, or components, nets, and buses. They are used during the schematics capture process in circuit design and once it has been created, it can then be passed to the printed circuit board design process. Mac gEDA. Linux gEDAFree. File used by Strater, a program used for visualizing subsurface borehole and well log data; specifies the nomenclature (keywords, data range, lithology, etc.) and the display properties (line, text, symbol, fill, etc.) for design elements that use the nomenclature; enables designs to be created according to standards. Strater schemes can be created and edited in the Scheme Editor, which is accessed by selecting Tools → Scheme Editor.. from the application menu. Windows Golden Software Strater. File created by the Shematic Capture Editor program included in KiCad, a tool suite used for designing PCB layouts and electronic schematics; saves an electronic schematic as it is laid out on the programs drawing canvas. Electronic schematics are used during the schematics capture process in circuit design. Once the electronic schematic has been created, it can then be passed to the printed circuit board design process. Windows KiCad. Mac KiCad. Linux KiCadFree. An SCH file contains a schematic, or visual diagram, of a printed circuit board PCB created with ExpressSCH design software. It stores an electronic schematic as it is laid out on the programs drawing canvas and includes symbols (for logic gates) connected by lines, which represent buses. SCH file open in ExpressSCH 7 The ExpressSCH Schematics (SCH) file type is one of several schematic file types that use the.sch file extension. The ExpressSCH file type is a proprietary file format that is not supported by other Schematics programs. You can only open an ExpressSCH file with ExpressSCH software. To open an SCH file with ExpressSCH, select File → Open.. To export an SCH file to a.BMP file with ExpressSCH, select File → Export schematic image.. Once a user finishes designing an electronic schematic, he passes it to the PCB design process. After the PCB is created, it is passed on to the manufacturing process to be assembled and put to use in various electronic products. NOTE: ExpressSCH is included with the ExpressPCB software package. Windows ExpressSCHFree.",
    "Windows Autodesk EAGLE. Altium Designer. Mac Autodesk EAGLE. Linux Autodesk EAGLE. Web Altium 365 Viewer. Mac Solutions Etcetera SuperCard. Solutions Etcetera SuperCard Help. Mac gEDA. Linux gEDA. Windows Golden Software Strater. Windows KiCad. Mac KiCad. Linux KiCad. Windows ExpressSCH.",
    "?"],
    ["cad_files",
    ".ART",
    "ArtCAM Model",
    "3.6",
    "CAD model created by ArtCAM, a CNC (computer numerical control) program used for artistic design and manufacturing; saves a 2D or 3D model as well as instructions for a machine to cut or engrave the design; used for signs, woodworking, engraving, and jewelry. Delcam ArtCAM is no longer developed. Windows Delcam ArtCAM. Bitmap image file compressed by America Online (AOL); saved in a proprietary format that most image viewing programs do not recognize; can be opened within America Online by selecting File→Open... To save an ART file in a more compatible format, open the image with AOL File Viewer, choose Save As.. and select a different format. Mac AOL Windows AOL ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. An ART file is an embroidery design created by versions 1 to 4 of BERNINA ARTlink, an embroidery application. It contains a design that includes object outlines, stitches, thread colors, a preview thumbnail image, and other metadata. ART files can be loaded into a BERNINA sewing machine and stitched onto a quilt, shirt, or another piece of fabric. ART file open in BERNINA ARTlink 8 The ART format is one of many design file types utilized in the embroidery community and is the native format used by BERNINA sewing machines and software. Other embroidery formats include.PES,.VP3,.VIP,.JEF,.HUS, and.PCS. There are several different versions of the ART format, and older versions of BERNINA software may not open newer versions of ART files. Also, beginning with version 5 of ARTlink, the software saves designs with file extensions that reflect the version of the software. For example, ARTlink 5 saves designs as.ART50 files, and ARTlink 6 saves designs as ART60 files. How do I transfer an ART file from my computer to a sewing machine? To transfer an ART file to a sewing machine, insert a USB storage device in your computer, then transfer the ART file from your computer to the connected storage device via File Explorer in Windows or Finder in macOS. After transferring the file, eject the storage device from your computer and insert it into the BERNINA sewing machine to transfer the design to embroider it onto the material. You can open and edit BERNINA ART files with the embroidery software included with BERNINA sewing machines. You can also be open, view, and print ART files with BERNINA ARTlink in Windows. If you are looking to convert an ART file to another embroidery format, you can do so with BERNINA ARTlink by selecting File → Export Machine File.. Conversion options include PES, JEF, SEW, PEC, VP3, VIP, HUS,.SHV, and.EXP. Windows BERNINA ARTlink. Image file that may have been created by several different drawing programs; typically a vector graphic and uses points, vertices, and lines to represent the image instead of dots like a bitmap image; also used by various clipart programs. Mac Adobe Illustrator 2023. Canon Crayola Windows Adobe Illustrator 2023. CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023. Canon Crayola. An ART file is an artwork project created by Visual Paradigm Online, a web app for designing documents, such as infographics and brochures. It is saved in the native Visual Paradigm Online Artwork (ART) format and contains document formatting, one or more layers, graphics, text, shapes, and other design elements. ART file open in Visual Paradigm Online Visual Paradigm Online is the online counterpart to the desktop Visual Paradigm application. The tool allows you to create, edit, save, export, and import artwork, such as infographics, flyers, posters, brochures, greeting cards, and resumes. How to create an ART file When you save artwork as an ART file with Visual Paradigm Online, you can choose to save it to local storage (your device) or Google Drive. After saving the file, you can import the file into Visual Paradigm Online to continue modifying the design. To create an ART file: Select File → Create New Design the artwork Select File → Save as.. Name the file and choose the save location (Google Drive or Device) NOTE: In Visual Paradigm Online, you can choose from different apps to create different types of artwork. When creating diagrams with the Diagram app module, Visual Paradigm Online saves diagrams as.VPD files. You can open an ART file with Visual Paradigm Online in a web browser. To open an ART file, select File → Open. Web Visual Paradigm OnlineFree. Visual Studio program bug description created with Artifacts, a file-based bug tracker; saved as an artifact with a unique ID and contains a bug description in an XML format; can be categorized and filtered by labels within Artifacts. Windows Versioned Artifacts.",
    "Windows Delcam ArtCAM. Mac AOL. Windows AOL ACD Systems ACDSee Photo Studio. Windows BERNINA ARTlink. Mac Adobe Illustrator 2023. Canon Crayola. Windows Adobe Illustrator 2023. CorelDRAW Graphics Suite 2023. Canon Crayola. Web Visual Paradigm Online. Windows Versioned Artifacts.",
    "Visual Paradigm Online can convert ART files to various image formats:.PDF - Portable Document Format.JPG - JPEG Image.PNG - Portable Network Graphic.SVG - Scalable Vector Graphics File."],
    ["cad_files",
    ".IF",
    "Procedimientos-Uno IFWin Project File",
    "3.6",
    "Project file created by IFWin, a program written in Spanish that is used for designing photovoltaic installations, which use solar cells to convert light into electric power; contains a 3D design, including the electrical components; used for planning photovoltaic structures before constructing them. Procedimientos-Uno discontinued IFWin. Windows Procedimientos-Uno IFWin.",
    "Windows Procedimientos-Uno IFWin.",
    "?"],
    ["cad_files",
    ".SVD",
    "SolidView Design File",
    "3.6",
    "Data file created by Polytec scanning vibrometer devices, which are used for measuring the durability of objects that are subjected to stresses and strains; contains a log of the data collected during a stress test; provided as input to PSV Software, a program that visualizes the stress results. Scanning vibrometers are used by test and simulation engineers to measure structural vibrations. Windows Polytec PSV Software. Audio file used by Roland keyboard synthesizers; contains patches, which are settings that fine tune the playback of a digital instrument; often used for storing instruments and effects; generally loaded onto a Roland synthesizer using a USB key. Windows Roland XV Editor. Mac Roland XV Editor. CAD file created by SolidView, a 2D and 3D computer-aided design software; saves the geometry and measurements for a part or an assembly; used by structural engineers, technical illustrators, manufacturing engineers, and other professionals for saving CAD designs. SVD files can be viewed with SolidView/Lite, a free program provided by Solid Concepts. The free software also provides the capability to measure the design. Windows Solid Concepts SolidView.",
    "Windows Polytec PSV Software. Windows Roland XV Editor. Mac Roland XV Editor. Windows Solid Concepts SolidView.",
    "?"],
    ["cad_files",
    ".CZD",
    "CAD Zone Drawing",
    "3.6",
    "A CZD file is a CAD document created by The Crash Zone or another CAD Zone software product. It contains a 3D model of an accident scene, crime scene, or other emergency situation. CZD files are used for sharing crash and other emergency diagrams that evaluate and influence road, site, and building construction. CAD Zone software products are used by crash investigators, firefighters, accident reconstructionists, law enforcement officers, and others. Windows The Crash Zone —  (Discontinued).",
    "Windows The Crash Zone —  (Discontinued).",
    "?"],
    ["cad_files",
    ".PRT",
    "CADKEY Part File",
    "3.6",
    "A PRT file is a part created by PTC Creo Parametric, which is part of the Creo CAD suite. It contains information used to record the parts structure and show it as a 3D model. Creo users often combine PRT files into Creo assembly (.ASM) files. Creo Parametric is a CAD program that engineers use to design manufactured parts and assemblies. Engineers can also use Creo to analyze the designs theyve created (e.g. test tolerances) and export the designs in formats used by Computer Numerical Control (CNC) machines. Parts created in Creo Parametric are saved as PRT files. While Creo is the primary application that uses PRT files, some other CAD applications can open them. NOTE: Creo Parametric was formerly known as Pro/Engineer and Wildfire. You can open a PRT file in PTC Creo (Windows) or Autodesk Fusion 360 (multiplatform). Note that you can open PRT files in only the Commerical version of Fusion 360; the Personal version does not support PRT files. All Platforms PTC Onshape. Windows PTC Creo. Okino Computer Graphics PolyTrans. Autodesk Fusion 360. Mac Autodesk Fusion 360. Linux PTC Creo. Web Autodesk Fusion 360. iOS Autodesk Fusion 360. Android Autodesk Fusion 360Free. Presentation template created by Corel Presentations, an application included with Corel WordPerfect Office; saves a slide style and layout that can be used for creating new.SHW presentations. Windows Corel Presentations 2021. CAD file created by CADKEY, a program used for designing 2D and 3D parts; contains both the model and drawing layouts; includes model geometry in wireframe, surface, and solids (ACIS based), plus dimensioning, annotation, vector, plane and other entity types in one modeling space. The Drawing Layout Mode in CADKEY contains defined views of model geometry for associative dimensioning and annotation, as well as section views. It also allows 2D wireframe geometry creation. NOTE: KeyCreator, the successor to CADKEY, uses.CKD files to store designs. Windows Kubotek CADKEY Kubotek Spectrum. A PRT file is a model part file saved in a three-dimensional model format used by Unigraphics, a 3D CAD program. It contains surface and solid information for a single part. PRT files are saved in a binary format, similar to an Alias wire model and an SDRC (Structural Dynamics Research Corporation) model. NOTE: Unigraphics was acquired by Siemens and is now distributed as Siemens NX. Windows Siemens NX Mac Siemens NX Linux Siemens NX. A PRT file contains portal information used by the Valve Visible Information Set (VVIS) command-line tool included with Hammer Editor, which is a program used to build maps for Valve games such as Half-Life. It stores a list of portals in ASCII format that are used by VVIS to perform visibility calculations to determine which objects on a map can be seen by a player and must be rendered. PRT file open in Apple TextEdit 1 PRT files are used to optimize maps/levels in Source engine games. The PRT files are generated by VBSP, which is a tool used to compile raw Valve Map.VMF files to the Binary Space Partition (BSP) format so that they can be used in BSP-based game engines. These.BSP maps must be completely sealed, meaning that they cannot connect to the black infinite area around the map. If the maps are not completely sealed, they will not work properly in the game. If the level is sealed, then VBSP creates a [mapname].prt file, which is then used by VVIS to calculate the visibility of objects and improve the performance of the map by communicating which objects must be rendered. If there is a leak in the map, then VBSP reports it and does not generate the PRT file, which causes VVIS to not perform the visibility calculations. NOTE: Since PRT files are saved in a text format, you can open them with a text editor, such as Microsoft Notepad or Apple TextEdit. However, you may have to change the.prt file extension to.txt to open it in the text editor. [mapname].prt - PRT files are named after the map/level for which they store portal information. An example of a PRT file name is d1_canals_06_d.prt. Windows Valve Hammer Editor. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. 3D model created with Solid Edge, a CAD program used primarily for creating industrial parts and assemblies; can be combined with other 3D parts in an assembly (.ASM) file. Windows Siemens Solid Edge. Contains configuration information that allows the computer to communicate with the printer; may be used by certain software programs, such as Dr. Halo software, which saves images in a device-independent format. Windows Referenced by the operating system. Output from a printing job sent to the printer and saved as a file; contains formatting information that tells the printer how the document should be printed. PRT files may be created on Unix systems using the FILEUTIL function with a Filename parameter. They can also be opened by FILEUTIL and printed using the LP (line printer) parameter. Windows Wasatch SoftRIP. Linux FILEUTIL. Protected text document created by Crypt Edit, a free program used for word processing; stores an encrypted and password protected document; may contain text, images, and page formatting information; used to securely store documents. NOTE: PolySoft Solutions discontinued development for Crypt Edit in 2000. Windows PolySoft Solutions Crypt Edit.",
    "All Platforms PTC Onshape. Windows PTC Creo. Okino Computer Graphics PolyTrans. Autodesk Fusion 360. Mac Autodesk Fusion 360. Linux PTC Creo. Web Autodesk Fusion 360. iOS Autodesk Fusion 360. Android Autodesk Fusion 360. Windows Corel Presentations 2021. Windows Kubotek CADKEY Kubotek Spectrum. Windows Siemens NX. Mac Siemens NX. Linux Siemens NX. Windows Valve Hammer Editor. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Mac Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Windows Siemens Solid Edge. Windows Referenced by the operating system. Windows Wasatch SoftRIP. Linux FILEUTIL. Windows PolySoft Solutions Crypt Edit.",
    "You can use the Commercial version of Autodesk Fusion 360 to convert PRT files to the following formats (and some others):.F3D - Fusion 360 Archive.3MF - 3D Manufacturing File.IPT - Autodesk Inventor Part.FBX - Autodesk FBX Interchange File.OBJ - Wavefront 3D Object.SKP - SketchUp Document.STP - STEP 3D CAD File.STL - Stereolithography File.USDZ - Universal Scene Description Zipped."],
    ["cad_files",
    ".DXX",
    "AutoCAD Drawing Interchange Attribute File",
    "3.6",
    "Data file created by AutoCAD, an application used for creating 3D design drawings; may contain drawing block reference, attribute, and end-of-sequence objects; can only store a subset of information that can be saved in a.DXF file. DXX files are used for extracting smaller amounts of information from a drawing that can be used interchangeably with other CAD applications. Windows Autodesk AutoCAD 2023.",
    "Windows Autodesk AutoCAD 2023.",
    "?"],
    ["cad_files",
    ".X_B",
    "Parasolid Model Part File",
    "3.6",
    "File created by Parasolid, a program for CAD geometric modeling; contains data such as geometry, topology, and color; designed as a standard exchange format for sharing CAD models; saved in binary format and may be imported or exported by other common CAD programs. X_B files are used in place of older version XMT_BIN and XMP_BIN files.X_T files store the same data as X_B files, but in text format. X_B files are used by the Parasolid standard, Translators, and Bodyshop editions. All Platforms PTC Onshape. Windows Siemens PLM Software Parasolid. Autodesk Fusion 360. Okino Computer Graphics PolyTrans. CADSoftTools CST CAD Navigator. Mac Siemens PLM Software Parasolid. Autodesk Fusion 360. CADSoftTools CST CAD Navigator. Linux Siemens PLM Software Parasolid. CADSoftTools CST CAD Navigator. Web Autodesk Fusion 360. iOS Autodesk Fusion 360. Android Autodesk Fusion 360Free.",
    "All Platforms PTC Onshape. Windows Siemens PLM Software Parasolid. Autodesk Fusion 360. Okino Computer Graphics PolyTrans. CADSoftTools CST CAD Navigator. Mac Siemens PLM Software Parasolid. Autodesk Fusion 360. CADSoftTools CST CAD Navigator. Linux Siemens PLM Software Parasolid. CADSoftTools CST CAD Navigator. Web Autodesk Fusion 360. iOS Autodesk Fusion 360. Android Autodesk Fusion 360.",
    "?"],
    ["cad_files",
    ".VWX",
    "Vectorworks Design File",
    "3.6",
    "2D or 3D design created with Vectorworks CAD software; created by Vectorworks 2008 and later; may contain two-dimensional drafting images or three-dimensional models. The Vectorworks suite includes the following programs: Designer - a multipurpose design solution Architect - for creating architectural designs Landmark - for site and landscape design Spotlight - a lighting design and simulation program Machine Design - for creating machine parts and mechanical systems Fundamentals - a flexible 3D modeling program RenderWorks - renders designs created Vectorworks software NOTE: The VWX format was introduced with Vectorworks 2008 and cannot be opened by Vectorworks 12.5 or earlier. Windows Nemetschek Vectorworks. Mac Nemetschek Vectorworks.",
    "Windows Nemetschek Vectorworks. Mac Nemetschek Vectorworks.",
    "?"],
    ["cad_files",
    ".FZZ",
    "Fritzing Shareable Project File",
    "3.5",
    "An FZZ file is a shareable project file created by Fritzing, an open-source electronics prototyping and design application. It is similar to a project file (.FZ file) but has been compressed so it can be shared among Fritzing users. Fritzing is a printed circuit board (PCB) design application that Arduino and other PCB enthusiasts use to create PCB layouts. Fritzing projects contain a digital representation of a real-world electronic circuit. Typically, Fritzing projects are saved as FZ files, but those who want to share their project with others can export the project as a compressed FZZ file. FZZ files contain every file a user needs to open and edit a project in Fritzing, including any custom parts (.FZPZ files) the project includes. This makes it easy for Fritzing users to share projects with each other, even if they do not have the same bins and parts installed in their separate instances of Fritzing. You can open an FZZ file in Fritzing, which is available for Windows, Mac, and Linux. To do so, open Fritzing, select File → Open.. from the programs menu bar, and then navigate to and open your FZZ file. Windows Fritzing. Mac Fritzing. Linux Fritzing.",
    "Windows Fritzing. Mac Fritzing. Linux Fritzing.",
    "?"],
    ["cad_files",
    ".CDW",
    "KOMPAS Document",
    "3.5",
    "CAD document created by KOMPAS-3D, a program used for modeling parts and assemblies; can be used for generating design documentation, technical illustrations, and for exporting model geometry for manufacturing. CDW files can be viewed with the free KOMPAS-3D Viewer. Windows ASCON KOMPAS-3D. ASCON KOMPAS-3D ViewerFree.",
    "Windows ASCON KOMPAS-3D. ASCON KOMPAS-3D Viewer.",
    "?"],
