    ["cad_files",
    ".UPF",
    "Unified Power Format File",
    "1.3",
    "Settings file created by MicroStation, a 3D CAD modeling tool; saves user preferences such as hotkeys, workspace settings, and the settings specified in the Workspace → Preferences dialog; enables preferences to be remembered. Windows Bentley Systems MicroStation. A UPF file contains 36 images captured by Panono, a 360-degree panoramic camera. It stores 36 images that are captured by Panonos 36 cameras and saved in the Unstitched Panorama Format (UPF). The Panono is a spherical camera that is thrown into the air in order to capture 360-degree images from a unique angle. When the device is at its highest point, the 36 cameras on the device capture 36 images, which are stored in the UPF file. The images are unstitched, but when viewed in the Panono Cloud are stitched together for a seamless 360-degree image. You can download UPF files from the Panono Cloud and stitch the individual images stored in a UPF file together with third party software or convert the images to.JPEG format with the Panono UPF Converter. Windows Panono UPF Converter. Mac Panono UPF Converter. Linux Panono UPF Converter. Web Panono Cloud. CAD file created in the Unified Power Format (UPF), a format used for annotating an electrical power design; can save information for power sources, power controls, and protection mechanisms; enables a power design to be documented. The UPF standard was developed by Accellera but then given over to IEEE. Windows Accellera load_upf.",
    "Windows Bentley Systems MicroStation. Windows Panono UPF Converter. Mac Panono UPF Converter. Linux Panono UPF Converter. Web Panono Cloud. Windows Accellera load_upf.",
    "?"],
    ["cad_files",
    ".CEL",
    "MicroStation Cell Library",
    "1.3",
    "A CEL file is a data file created by Affymetrix DNA microarray image analysis software. It contains the data extracted from probes on an Affymetrix GeneChip and can store thousands of data points, which may make it large in file size. CEL files can be processed by software algorithms and visualized on a 2D grid as part of an overall genome experiment. An Affymetrix GeneChip is a biological chip that contains a microarray which is valid for one experiment. To create these chips, a glass or silicon slide is arrayed with probes, which report expression levels (intensities) as perfect match (PM) and mismatch (MM) values, based on whether they are complementary to the original DNA sample. These values may be used for studying DNA alterations, called single-nucleotide polymorphisms (SNPs), which are used in human and animal disease research. The CEL file format has multiple versions, which use different formatting. For example, version 3 uses ASCII text formatting while version 4 uses a binary format. NOTE: CEL files require a corresponding.CDF file, which is the dictionary for the raw probe-level data stored in the CEL file. MATLAB has a built-in function called affyread that can be used to read CEL files in the Windows version of the software. Windows Affymetrix Tiling Analysis Software. The MathWorks MATLAB. VSN GenStat. RMAExpress. dChip. multi-aff-py. Mac multi-aff-py. Linux multi-aff-pyFree. Script used by Celestia, a free space browsing application; written using a specific Celestia syntax and includes commands for moving the viewing perspective throughout the universe; used for creating 3D universe tours. CEL files may also include more advanced features, such as instructions to load custom 3D models into the space tour. They can also include captions to provide interesting facts to the observer. If you download or receive a CEL file, you can open it by double-clicking the file, or by selecting File → Run Script.. from the application menu and then choosing the CEL file. The CEL format has been replaced by the.CELX format in recent versions of Celestia. However, Celestia still supports CEL files. The newer CELX format uses the Lua scripting language, which is more expressive and powerful than the CEL language. NOTE: CEL files are saved as plain text files and are edited using a text editor. Windows Celestia. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Other text editor Mac Celestia. Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Other text editor Linux Celestia. GNU Emacs. Other text editor. Audio file used by Adobe Audition, an audio production application; saves an audio loop that was originally in the.MP3 format but was modified by the software so is it suitable for looping. Adobe Audition includes several royalty free loops with the software installation. NOTE: Audition no longer supports CEL files. Windows Earlier versions of Adobe Audition. Cell library created by MicroStation, a CAD program used to create 2D and 3D design drafts; stores the geometry, symbols, and other draft information for an object; used to store the building blocks for generating higher-order designs. CEL files can be exported to.DWG and.DXF formats using MicroStation. Windows Bentley Systems MicroStation. Oracle AutoVue. File used by Battery 3, a program that creates drum rhythms and sounds; contains sound properties for a particular drum sound within a Battery 3 drum sound cell; used to modify drum samples with additional effects, such as reverb, tone, or compression. Windows Native Instruments Battery 3 Mac Native Instruments Battery 3. A CEL file is an animation saved in the FLIC animation format, most popularly used by Autodesk Animator and Animator Pro. It contains a series of computer-generated frames. CEL files are compressed using lossless RLE compression. Autodesk Animator is a 2D animation program that Autodesk released in 1989 for MS-DOS. The program was succeeded by Animator Pro, which Autodesk released in 1991. In most cases, Animator and Animator Pro saved animations users created as.FLI and.FLC files, respectively. However, some Animator and Animator Pro animations are instead saved as CEL files. CEL files are identical to FLI and FLC files, except they contain an additional chunk of data in the formats optional file header. You can open a CEL file with Corel VideoStudio (Windows), Apple QuickTime Player (Mac), or XAnim (Linux). You may have to change the files extension to.fli or.flc before you can open it. Windows Corel VideoStudio 2022. Mac Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. Linux XAnimFree.",
    "Windows Affymetrix Tiling Analysis Software. The MathWorks MATLAB. VSN GenStat. RMAExpress. dChip. multi-aff-py. Mac multi-aff-py. Linux multi-aff-py. Windows Celestia. Microsoft Notepad Included with OS. Other text editor. Mac Celestia. Apple TextEdit Included with OS. Other text editor. Linux Celestia. GNU Emacs. Other text editor. Windows Earlier versions of Adobe Audition. Windows Bentley Systems MicroStation. Oracle AutoVue. Windows Native Instruments Battery 3. Mac Native Instruments Battery 3. Windows Corel VideoStudio 2022. Mac Apple QuickTime Player Included with OS. Linux XAnim.",
    "?"],
