    "1.0",
    "Settings file created using Connection Manager, a suite of software components that enables system administrators to setup Windows remote connection profiles; saves information such as the username, password, and the phone number to dial. CMP files enable administrators to configure initial settings for a users dial-up connection. NOTE: The Connection Manager Administration Kit (CMAK) is the name of the Connection Manager tool used for setting up profiles. Windows Microsoft Connection Manager Administration Kit. Text module created using HotDocs digital form preparation software; saves a clause which contains text as well as HotDocs components (e.g., form fields); provides a reusable object for insertion into HotDocs templates (.HFT or.HPT files). Clauses can either be specific to a template or to a clause library (.HDL file). For example, if you create a clause while editing a HotDocs template, it will be added to the templates CMP component file. Windows HotDocs. Wire harness designed with Siemens Solid Edge Wire Harness Design, an eCAD program; contains the wire routing and cable harness design used for organizing wires in a 3D assembly (.ASM) file. Solid Edge provides live feedback for design violations in CMP files, which prevents incorrect wiring of devices. Windows Siemens Solid Edge. Drawing component created with Generic CADD, an older CAD program developed for Windows; used for storing vector objects that can be inserted in a Generic CADD drawing (.GCD) file. NOTE: Generic CADD has been replaced by General CADD Pro (GCP), which saves components as.GXC files. CMP files can be opened by both Generic CADD and General CADD Pro. Windows General CADD Pro. Generic CADD. A CMP file is a character pose created by Concept Matrix, a Final Fantasy XIV (FFXIV) character posing tool. It contains data used to apply a custom pose to a players FFXIV character. After loading a CMP file, players can take a screenshot of their custom-posed character. Final Fantasy XIV is a massively multiplayer online role-playing game (MMORPG) published by Square Enix. In the game, players take on the role of an adventurer exploring the fictional world of Eorzea. FFXIV modders have created several tools that allow them to alter the games gameplay and add custom features. Concept Matrix and its successor, Anamnesis, are tools that allow a player to alter their characters pose to take posed screenshots. If a player wants to save a character pose theyve created in Concept Matrix, they can select Posing Matrix → Save & Load → Save CMP File. This saves the pose as a CMP file, which can be loaded into either Concept Matrix or Anamnesis. NOTE: Anamesis saves poses as POSE files. Concept Matrix cannot load POSE files. You can open a CMP file with Concept Matrix (Windows) or Anamesis (Windows). Note that to use these tools, you must also have Final Fantasy XIV (Windows) installed and running. To open a CMP file in Concept Matrix, select Posing Matrix → Save & Load → Load CMP File. Windows Concept Matrix. AnamnesisFree.",
